body:
@KeyboardDanni The callback mode for SkeletonModifier depends on Skeleton3D's `modifier_callback_mode_process`, so it is already implemented.

To further improve interpolation during the physics_process, one could consider integrating `physics_interpolation` not only into Node3D.transform but also into the transform API provided by Skeleton3D.pose.

Regarding the FPS dependent issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229, as mentioned in there, it's difficult to improve using SpringBone's integration-based algorithm. While caching two or more frames might be able to try (derivative of velocity) based improvements, we won't know until we run experiments.
